WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.700
- In the time of COVID, it's
always refreshing to get out

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.730
and see friends, as long
as we can do it safely.

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:07.290
That's why we've created a segment

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:09.623
called the Drive-INterview, get it?

00:00:11.305 --> 00:00:14.138
♪ Drive-Interview ♪

00:00:15.902 --> 00:00:17.530
- (laughs)The wink, I love you.

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:19.590
Recently, I had a chance to catch up

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:20.850
with Cedric the Entertainer

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:22.330
at our good ole outdoor theater.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:23.774
Check this out.

00:00:23.774 --> 00:00:26.357
(upbeat music)

00:00:39.074 --> 00:00:40.400
What's up, Cedric?

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:41.233
- What up, Kelly?

00:00:41.233 --> 00:00:42.066
How are you?

00:00:42.066 --> 00:00:44.570
Hey, oh, wait a minute, are
we a socially distanced?

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:45.630
Are we six feet apart?

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:48.190
- Oh man, okay, well, I've
been traveling with this.

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:52.136
I think we're good, but like,
let's just check it out.

00:00:52.136 --> 00:00:53.920
Now maybe don't touch it,

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.520
'cause I don't know how
many tests you've had.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:57.014
- You're right there, that's already good.

00:00:57.014 --> 00:00:58.110
- But we're already good, we're good.

00:00:58.110 --> 00:00:59.020
- That's already good.

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:00.690
- It's kind of a little floppy, this one

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:03.410
That didn't work out so well.
- Nice car.

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:04.980
- Do you like drive-ins?

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:05.980
- Yeah, yeah. I love it.

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:09.260
I've loved cars since I was younger.

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:12.180
Now, I used to have cars that
I would work on and like fix,

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.267
but you know, I kind of
became real Hollywood,

00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:16.667
and then my manicures
started getting messed up.

00:01:17.861 --> 00:01:19.290
- (laughs) And then you
didn't have time for it.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:21.400
- I was like whoa, wait a minute,

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:22.970
I'm not gonna be having dirty nails.

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:25.390
Let me get a guy, let me get a car guy.

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:26.223
- A car guy.

00:01:26.223 --> 00:01:27.290
- Yeah, everybody's got a guy.

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:28.270
I got a guy for you.

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:29.887
- Actually, Jay Leno has been my car guy.

00:01:29.887 --> 00:01:31.781
- Oh, well then you got
super guy, you got the guy.

00:01:31.781 --> 00:01:32.911
- I know, I did his show and
I was like, wait a minute,

00:01:32.911 --> 00:01:34.830
so I have this 49 Ford truck,

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:35.900
can you help me out with it?

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:37.680
He's so awesome.

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:38.635
Have you ever done anything interesting

00:01:38.635 --> 00:01:39.468
in the back of a car?

00:01:39.468 --> 00:01:40.658
I mean, I don't know.

00:01:40.658 --> 00:01:43.540
- Well, you know, driving from college,

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:46.780
we used to drive like
two hours from St. Louis

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:49.700
to my little college town
in Cape Girardeau, Missouri.

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:51.550
And one time it was like a group of us,

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:55.200
we tried to play Monopoly
in the car, with the board.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.000
Like nowadays, these
kids got an app I'm sure,

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.880
they can just play on an
app and phone to phone.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:02.140
But we had the board out,

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:03.698
and then whenever my friend would stop

00:02:03.698 --> 00:02:06.867
all the houses would
slide off and you would-

00:02:06.867 --> 00:02:07.700
- I'm gonna be real with you.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:09.880
You led with, man in college,

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:12.270
and I thought that story
was going somewhere else,

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:15.025
with the back of a car, and
then you brought up Monopoly.

00:02:15.025 --> 00:02:16.885
- Yeah no, no, it didn't get

00:02:16.885 --> 00:02:18.380
much sexier than a game of Monopoly.

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:19.213
- It doesn't get much sexier

00:02:19.213 --> 00:02:21.870
than getting Boardwalk and Park Place.

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:23.695
- The Community Chest, that
was the most chest we saw.

00:02:23.695 --> 00:02:25.970
- That's actually amazing.

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:26.970
So tell me about your new project.

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:28.760
You have a new project
called "The Opening Act"?

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:30.970
- Yeah, "The Opening
Act" is a great movie.

00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:32.750
It's really about what it is

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:35.323
to be a standup comedian, how it starts.

00:02:35.323 --> 00:02:37.330
I play a character called Billy G.

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:40.220
He's like a old school veteran comic.

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:42.380
And then Jimmy O. Yang is in it

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:44.880
as this young comedian
trying to find his way

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:47.380
and make that choice
from whatever he's doing

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:50.620
in regular life to try
and to like be a comedian

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:51.650
for the rest of his life.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:54.540
And so the movie captures it all.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:57.730
And so many great comics
that decided to be a part

00:02:57.730 --> 00:03:00.480
of it because of the way
movie is written, so.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.410
- That's a hard thing,

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:03.100
especially when you're not anyone yet.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.940
Now you go anywhere and
everybody was ready to laugh

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:06.630
with you 'cause they
know you're hilarious.

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:08.340
But like in the beginning,
that must have been hard.

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:09.173
- Yeah, no, it is.

00:03:09.173 --> 00:03:11.750
It's one of those things where you don't,

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.390
you know, 'cause all your
friends are going like,

00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:15.181
man, you're funny, you
should do it, you know?

00:03:15.181 --> 00:03:17.882
But to go up into a crowd you don't know,

00:03:17.882 --> 00:03:19.530
and like have to perform it,

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:21.430
and then do it night after night,

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.780
and of course, you're gonna
bomb up there sometime.

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:25.370
And this movie shows all of that.

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:27.140
Well, let's see a little
bit of "Opening Act".

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.490
We're at a drive-in, so
let's see a little bit of it.

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:30.433
- All right, check it out.
- All right.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:33.060
- Find your voice.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:36.514
You find your voice, your
audience will find you.

00:03:36.514 --> 00:03:38.793
That's when you're competing.

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:42.603
- What about you?

00:03:42.603 --> 00:03:43.909
- The funny thing is,
when I first started this

00:03:43.909 --> 00:03:47.920
I used to think that I
had to make them laugh

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:49.950
so that I could feel good.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:53.930
But over time, I realized
that I make them laugh

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:55.800
so that they feel good.

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:58.310
It's the best job in the world.

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:01.730
- Oh my gosh, I can't wait.

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:02.563
- Do you remember,

00:04:02.563 --> 00:04:03.410
speaking to that, like the beginning,

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:05.750
do you ever remember your
worst gig you ever had?

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:08.400
Well, man, I had a tough
gig with Sam Kinison,

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.740
the late, great Sam Kinison, super funny.

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:13.570
Very rowdy-
- Loud.

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:14.540
- Loud.
- Yeah.

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:16.760
- He had a show, I was
in Des Moines, Iowa.

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:18.060
The crowd was there for him.

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:20.013
They were fired up, they were rowdy.

00:04:20.013 --> 00:04:22.910
And then they told me to stretch.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:24.570
The set wasn't ready.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:26.390
And I was on stage eating it, man.

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:28.543
That was like tough, man.

00:04:28.543 --> 00:04:29.376
That was so tough.

00:04:29.376 --> 00:04:30.209
- You think that people do that

00:04:30.209 --> 00:04:31.250
to other comedians on purpose?

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.470
Like with musicians,
you kinda, I don't know,

00:04:33.470 --> 00:04:34.430
There's always like other songs,

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:36.160
it's not like a whole thing.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:38.270
There's no callbacks, really,
like when it comes to comedy.

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:39.640
Do you think he did that on purpose?

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:43.111
- You know, it's Sam Kinison,
I think he was just drunk.

00:04:43.111 --> 00:04:45.100
Let's just be honest.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:46.123
- Well, I love it.

00:04:47.719 --> 00:04:50.360
All right, well, hey,
we've got to do this again.

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:51.810
- We do, I love meeting up like this.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:52.800
You know what it's like?

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:55.002
It's like an old detective
movie where we got like,

00:04:55.002 --> 00:04:56.390
I got some stuff,

00:04:56.390 --> 00:04:58.850
maybe I dropped some
stuff off in the trunk.

00:04:58.850 --> 00:04:59.683
And then you say hey-

00:04:59.683 --> 00:05:01.191
